    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "DOGGO was exploited on Ethereum Mainnet on September 20, 2024, with the attacker draining ~$7,000 by manipulating the token contract’s self-balance threshold via flash loans and swaps, triggering a flawed branch in transfer logic. The DOGGO token contract’s transfer logic used its own self-balance (balanceOf(address(this))) as a conditional branch. The attacker used flash loans and swaps to manipulate this balance below a threshold, triggering a special branch, enabling favorable swap behavior and draining value."
